{"name":"Sweet Alyssum","hex":"#e7c2de","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet alyssum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A low-growing flowering annual (Lobularia maritima)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_alyssum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Alyssum (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Alyssum is a 1915 American silent drama film directed by Colin Campbell and starring Tyrone Power Sr., Kathlyn Williams, and Edith Johnson. A print of Sweet Alyssum exists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Sweet_Alyssum_%28film%29.jpg/330px-Sweet_Alyssum_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Alyssum_(film)"},{"title":"Lobularia maritima","blocks":[{"text":"Lobularia maritima is a species of low-growing flowering plant in the family Brassicaceae. Its common name is sweet alyssum or sweet Alison, also commonly referred to as just alyssum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Smagliczka_nadmorska_1.jpg/330px-Smagliczka_nadmorska_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lobularia_maritima"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Alyssum","blocks":[{"text":"Alyssum is a genus of over a hundred species of flowering plants in the family Brassicaceae, native to temperate Europe, Asia, and northern Africa, with the highest species diversity in the Mediterranean region. The genus comprises annual and perennial herbaceous plants or (rarely) small shrubs, growing to 10–100 cm tall, with oblong-oval leaves. Alyssum flowers are characteristically small and grouped in terminal clusters; they are often yellow or white colored but can be pink or purple."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Alyssum_montanum_ENBLA06.jpg/330px-Alyssum_montanum_ENBLA06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alyssum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sweet_alyssum.jpg/500px-Sweet_alyssum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sweet_alyssum.jpg/500px-Sweet_alyssum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cultivar 'White Alyssum'","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweet_alyssum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG/120px-Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG/250px-Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG/120px-Brassicaceae_-_Lobularia_maritima.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en